<title>GERMANY: SGL Carbon shares slip after 1996 results.</title>
<headline>SGL Carbon shares slip after 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German carbon and graphite maker SGL Carbon AG slipped after the group reported provisional 1996 results.</p>
<p>SGL Carbon, the world's leading graphite maker, said its operating profit jumped 25 percent to 324 million marks while sales were up 13 percent to 1.78 billion marks.</p>
<p>Shares slipped 50 pfennigs to 212.50 marks, while the broader IBIS 30-share DAX index was up 0.66 percent at 3,038.56 points.</p>
<p>Dealers said some of the losses were due to profit-taking.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
